IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwr-common`

-- Fair Work Regulations 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: what a person bringing a claim to the Fair Work Commission or a
-- court meets in the regulations. Absence for illness or injury as a protected reason (regs 3.01, 6.04); the application
-- fees, the hardship waiver and the refund (regs 3.02, 3.03, 3.07, 3A.03, 3A.05, 6.05, 6.07A); defence members and stop
-- sexual harassment orders (reg 3.29A); choosing the small claims procedure and who may represent you in it (reg 4.01);
-- other proceedings that bar an unfair deactivation or termination application (regs 6.01A, 6.01B).
--
-- Seat: the claimant -- the dismissed employee, the bullied or harassed worker, the regulated worker deactivated or
-- terminated, the employee suing for unpaid amounts.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 57 (F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.
-- Not deposited, so inputs: the CPI index numbers (the indexation formula itself is lost from the deposited text, NOTES.md
-- finding 1), the fee figures published for each year, the Fair Work Commission's satisfaction, rules of court.

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the FWC`, `the applicant`
DECLARE `Fee action` IS ONE OF
    `repay the fee` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER

§ `regs 3.01, 6.04 -- absence because of illness or injury (only if you were dismissed while off sick or injured)`

-- Reg 3.01 (for s 352 of the Act, a general protection) and reg 6.04 (for s 772(1)(a), unlawful termination) prescribe
-- the kinds of illness or injury for which an employer must not dismiss a temporarily absent employee.
-- (2): one exists "if the employee provides a medical certificate ... or a statutory declaration ... within: (a) 24
-- hours after the commencement of the absence; or (b) such longer period as is reasonable in the circumstances."
-- (3): one exists if the employee "(a) is required by the terms of a workplace instrument: (i) to notify the employer of
-- an absence from work; and (ii) to substantiate the reason for the absence; and (b) complies with those terms."
-- Reg 3.01(4) only: one exists "if the employee has provided the employer with evidence, in accordance with paragraph
-- 107(3)(a) of the Act, for taking paid personal/carer's leave for a personal illness or personal injury". Reg 6.04 has
-- no such route (NOTES.md finding 3).
-- Reg 3.01(5) / 6.04(4): it "is not a prescribed kind ... if: (a) either: (i) the employee's absence extends for more
-- than 3 months; or (ii) the total absences ... within a 12 month period, have been more than 3 months ...; and (b) the
-- employee is not on paid personal/carer's leave ... for the duration of the absence."
-- Reg 3.01(6) / 6.04(5): paid personal/carer's leave "does not include a period when the employee is absent from work
-- while receiving compensation under a law ... about workers' compensation".
-- Answers: JUST FALSE where (5) / (4) says "is not"; JUST TRUE where a route is met; otherwise NOTHING (the routes are
-- introduced by "exists if", not "only if", so the regulation does not say no).
GIVEN `for section 352` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hours after the absence began that I gave a certificate or declaration` IS A NUMBER,
      `I gave a certificate or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I complied with those terms` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for my illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day my absence began` IS A DATE,
      `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` IS A DATE,
      `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the illness or injury is of a prescribed kind` MEANS
    IF `the long-absence exclusion applies` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF    `the certificate route`
            OR `the instrument route`
            OR (`for section 352` AND `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for my illness or injury`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the certificate route` MEANS
                `I gave a certificate or declaration`
            AND (   `hours after the absence began that I gave a certificate or declaration` AT MOST 24
                 OR `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances`)
        `the instrument route` MEANS
                `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence`
            AND `I complied with those terms`
        `the long-absence exclusion applies` MEANS
                (   `lasts more than` `the day my absence began` `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` 3
                 OR `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months`)
            AND (NOT (`I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` AND (NOT `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence`)))

@export Was my illness or injury of a kind that protects my absence from dismissal under the general protections (s 352, reg 3.01)?
GIVEN `I gave a certificate or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer a medical certificate or a statutory declaration about the illness or injury
      `hours after the absence began that I gave it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after your absence began you gave the certificate or declaration
      `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave it after 24 hours: whether that longer period was reasonable in the circumstances
      `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award or agreement required you to notify your employer of an absence and substantiate the reason
      `I complied with those terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with those terms
      `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for my illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer the evidence required (s 107(3)(a)) to take paid personal leave for your illness or injury
      `the day my absence began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your absence
      `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc The day your absence ended, or the day you were dismissed if it had not ended
      `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absences within a 12 month period added up to more than 3 months
      `I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were on paid personal (sick) leave for the whole of the absence
      `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving workers compensation during any of the absence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my illness or injury protected under s 352` IS
    `the illness or injury is of a prescribed kind` TRUE `hours after the absence began that I gave it` `I gave a certificate or declaration` `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances` `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence` `I complied with those terms` `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for my illness or injury` `the day my absence began` `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months` `I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence`

@export Was my illness or injury of a kind that protects my absence from termination under the unlawful termination rules (s 772(1)(a), reg 6.04)?
GIVEN `I gave a certificate or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer a medical certificate or a statutory declaration about the illness or injury
      `hours after the absence began that I gave it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after your absence began you gave the certificate or declaration
      `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave it after 24 hours: whether that longer period was reasonable in the circumstances
      `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award or agreement required you to notify your employer of an absence and substantiate the reason
      `I complied with those terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with those terms
      `the day my absence began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your absence
      `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc The day your absence ended, or the day your employment was terminated if it had not ended
      `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absences within a 12 month period added up to more than 3 months
      `I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were on paid personal (sick) leave for the whole of the absence
      `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving workers compensation during any of the absence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my illness or injury protected under s 772` IS
    `the illness or injury is of a prescribed kind` FALSE `hours after the absence began that I gave it` `I gave a certificate or declaration` `if a longer period was reasonable in the circumstances` `an instrument required me to notify and substantiate the absence` `I complied with those terms` FALSE `the day my absence began` `the day my absence ended or I was dismissed` `my absences in a 12 month period totalled more than 3 months` `I was on paid personal leave for the whole absence` `I was receiving workers compensation during the absence`

§ `application fees -- regs 3.02, 3.03, 3.07, 3A.03, 3A.05, 6.05, 6.07A`

DECLARE `Application to the FWC` IS ONE OF
    `a general protections dismissal dispute (s 365)`
    `a general protections dispute not about dismissal (s 372)`
    `an unfair dismissal remedy (Part 3-2)`
    `an unlawful termination dispute (s 773)`
    `a stop bullying order (s 789FC)`
    `an unfair deactivation or termination remedy (s 536LU)`
    `a review of a services contract (s 536ND)`

-- The fee at commencement, (2) of each regulation: regs 3.02, 3.03, 3.07, 6.05: "If the application is made in the
-- financial year starting on 1 July 2009, the fee is $59.50." Regs 3A.03, 3A.05: "in the financial year starting on 1
-- July 2024, the fee is $87.20." Reg 6.07A: "on or after 1 January 2014 but before 1 July 2014, the fee is $65.50."
@export What was the application fee when the fee regulation for my kind of application began (regs 3.02(2), 3.03(2), 3.07(2), 3A.03(2), 3A.05(2), 6.05(2), 6.07A(2))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC` @desc Which application you are making to the Fair Work Commission
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What was the starting application fee` IS
    CONSIDER `my application`
    WHEN `a stop bullying order (s 789FC)` THEN 65.50
    WHEN `an unfair deactivation or termination remedy (s 536LU)` THEN 87.20
    WHEN `a review of a services contract (s 536ND)` THEN 87.20
    OTHERWISE 59.50

-- The first financial year (by the calendar year it starts in) to which the starting fee applies; reg 6.07A's half-year
-- from 1 January 2014 is counted as the financial year starting 1 July 2013.
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the starting fee applies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my application`
    WHEN `a stop bullying order (s 789FC)` THEN 2013
    WHEN `an unfair deactivation or termination remedy (s 536LU)` THEN 2024
    WHEN `a review of a services contract (s 536ND)` THEN 2024
    OTHERWISE 2009

-- (3): "(a) identify the amount of the fee for an application made in the previous financial year; (b) multiply it by
-- the indexation factor for the application year ...; (c) round the result to the nearest multiple of 10 cents, rounding
-- up if the result ends in 5 cents." (5): the factor is "rounded up or down to 3 decimal places, rounding up if the
-- result ends in 0.0005". The factor's formula (4) is lost from the deposited text, so the factor is an input; it is
-- rounded here as (5) says. Reg 6.05(3)(c) and (5) say "if the result is 5 cents" and "if the result is 0.0005" instead
-- of "ends in" (NOTES.md finding 2); the "ends in" reading is applied to every kind.
@export What is this financial year's application fee, worked out from last year's fee and the indexation factor (the fee regulations, subregulations (3) and (5))?
GIVEN `last financial year's fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The fee for an application made in the previous financial year, in dollars
      `this year's indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexation factor for this financial year worked out from the CPI under subregulation (4) (for example 1.0384)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is this year's application fee` IS
    `rounded to the nearest 10 cents` (`last financial year's fee` TIMES (`rounded to 3 decimal places` `this year's indexation factor`))

-- (7): "If the FWC is satisfied that the person making an application will suffer serious hardship if the person is
-- required to pay the fee, no fee is payable for making the application." Answered conditionally on the FWC.
@export How much application fee must I pay (the fee regulations, subregulation (7))?
GIVEN `this year's fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The application fee for this financial year, in dollars
      `if the FWC is satisfied I would suffer serious hardship paying it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied you would suffer serious hardship if you had to pay the fee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much application fee must I pay` IS
    IF `if the FWC is satisfied I would suffer serious hardship paying it` THEN 0 ELSE `this year's fee`

§ `the fee refund when you discontinue (only if you paid a fee and then discontinued)`

-- (8) of regs 3.02, 3.03, 3A.03, 3A.05, 6.05: "The FWC must repay to the person an amount equal to the fee if: (a) the
-- fee has been paid; and (b) the application is subsequently discontinued as mentioned in section 588 of the Act; and
-- (c) either: (i) at the time the application is discontinued, the application has not yet been listed for conducting a
-- [conference / conciliation, conference or hearing]; or (ii) if the application has ... been listed ... on a specified
-- date or dates--the discontinuance occurs at least 2 days before that date or the earlier of those dates."
-- Reg 3.07(8) puts the same test as "a circumstance in which the FWC must refund", which does not close the list: when
-- it fails, NOTHING. Reg 6.07A(8)(c) has only the "not yet listed" limb: no two-day rule (NOTES.md finding 3).
-- Which listings count: a conference only, for regs 3.02, 3.03, 6.05; a conciliation, conference or hearing, for regs
-- 3.07, 3A.03, 3A.05; a conference or hearing, for reg 6.07A.
-- READING (NOTES.md finding 6): "at least 2 days before" is read as two clear days between the discontinuance and the
-- listed date (the listed date at least 3 days after). The other reading (2 days after is enough) is in the fork register.
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC`, `listed for a conference` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `listed for a conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN, `listed for a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a listing that counts was made` IF
    CONSIDER `my application`
    WHEN `a general protections dismissal dispute (s 365)` THEN `listed for a conference`
    WHEN `a general protections dispute not about dismissal (s 372)` THEN `listed for a conference`
    WHEN `an unlawful termination dispute (s 773)` THEN `listed for a conference`
    WHEN `a stop bullying order (s 789FC)` THEN `listed for a conference` OR `listed for a hearing`
    OTHERWISE `listed for a conference` OR `listed for a conciliation` OR `listed for a hearing`

GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC`, `I paid the fee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I discontinued under s 588` IS A BOOLEAN, `listed for a conference` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `listed for a conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN, `listed for a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day I discontinued` IS A DATE, `the earliest listed day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the refund conditions are met` MEANS
    IF `met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `my application` EQUALS `an unfair dismissal remedy (Part 3-2)` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `listed` MEANS `a listing that counts was made` `my application` `listed for a conference` `listed for a conciliation` `listed for a hearing`
        `two clear days before` MEANS `days from` `the day I discontinued` `the earliest listed day` AT LEAST 3
        `timing is met` MEANS
            IF (NOT `listed`) THEN TRUE
            ELSE IF `my application` EQUALS `a stop bullying order (s 789FC)` THEN FALSE
                 ELSE `two clear days before`
        `met` MEANS `I paid the fee` AND `I discontinued under s 588` AND `timing is met`

-- The FWC's duty, as a regulative rule: where the conditions are met, the FWC must repay an amount equal to the fee. The
-- text gives no time for the repayment, so the rule has no WITHIN.
GIVEN `the fee paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Fee action`
`the FWC's duty to repay the fee` MEANS
    PARTY `the FWC`
    MUST  `repay the fee` (EXACTLY `the fee paid`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the FWC` BECAUSE "the fee was not repaid after the application was discontinued in time"

@export Must the Fair Work Commission repay my application fee because I discontinued my application (regs 3.02(8), 3.03(8), 3.07(8), 3A.03(8), 3A.05(8), 6.05(8), 6.07A(8))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC` @desc Which application you made to the Fair Work Commission
      `I paid the fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the application fee
      `I discontinued under s 588` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you discontinued the application (s 588 of the Act)
      `it had been listed for a conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a conference
      `it had been listed for a conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a conciliation
      `it had been listed for a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a hearing
      `the day I discontinued` IS A DATE @desc The day you discontinued the application
      `the earliest listed day` IS A DATE @desc The earliest date it was listed for (a conference, conciliation or hearing); any date if it was not listed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fee be repaid` IS
    `the refund conditions are met` `my application` `I paid the fee` `I discontinued under s 588` `it had been listed for a conference` `it had been listed for a conciliation` `it had been listed for a hearing` `the day I discontinued` `the earliest listed day`

@export How much of my application fee must be repaid because I discontinued (the fee regulations, subregulation (8))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application to the FWC` @desc Which application you made to the Fair Work Commission
      `the fee I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The application fee you paid, in dollars (0 if you paid none)
      `I discontinued under s 588` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you discontinued the application (s 588 of the Act)
      `it had been listed for a conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a conference
      `it had been listed for a conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a conciliation
      `it had been listed for a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the time you discontinued, the application had been listed for a hearing
      `the day I discontinued` IS A DATE @desc The day you discontinued the application
      `the earliest listed day` IS A DATE @desc The earliest date it was listed for; any date if it was not listed
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much fee must be repaid` IS
    CONSIDER `the refund conditions are met` `my application` (`the fee I paid` GREATER THAN 0) `I discontinued under s 588` `it had been listed for a conference` `it had been listed for a conciliation` `it had been listed for a hearing` `the day I discontinued` `the earliest listed day`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the fee I paid`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `reg 3.29A -- defence members and stop sexual harassment orders (only if you were a defence member when harassed)`

-- Act s 527F(3): a person "cannot, except as provided by the regulations, apply for the FWC to make a stop sexual
-- harassment order ... if the aggrieved person was a defence member ... at the time the sexual harassment allegedly
-- occurred." Reg 3.29A(2): not prevented "if at least one of the respondents ...: (a) was not a defence member at the
-- time the contravention allegedly occurred; or (b) is not a defence member at the time the application is made."
-- (3): also not prevented if a respondent was a defence member then "and at least one of the following circumstances
-- exist: (a) in response to a request by the aggrieved person under section 46 of the Defence Regulations 2026 for a
-- review ...: (i) a stop sexual harassment direction is not issued ...; or (ii) a ... direction is issued ..., and the
-- person is dissatisfied with the direction; (b) the person is not eligible to use the process under Part 7 of the
-- Defence Regulations 2026 to resolve the dispute; (c) the process ... is available ... but is not suitable because: (i)
-- a respondent ... would be involved in conducting the process; and (ii) there is no other person that is authorised or
-- empowered under that Part to conduct the process in place of the respondent."
-- Answers: NOTHING if the aggrieved person was not a defence member (the bar and the regulation do not arise; s 527F(1)
-- governs); JUST TRUE if a circumstance exists; JUST FALSE otherwise (the s 527F(3) bar, a flat "cannot").
@export Can I apply to the Fair Work Commission for a stop sexual harassment order although I was a defence member when harassed (s 527F(3), reg 3.29A)?
GIVEN `I was a defence member when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a defence member (Defence Force Discipline Act 1982) when the sexual harassment allegedly happened
      `a respondent was not a defence member then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one person who harassed you was not a defence member at the time
      `a respondent is not a defence member now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one person who harassed you is not a defence member now, when you apply
      `my Defence review request got no direction or one I am dissatisfied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on your request for review under s 46 of the Defence Regulations 2026, no stop sexual harassment direction was issued, or one was issued and you are dissatisfied with it
      `I am not eligible for the Defence Part 7 process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not eligible to use the process under Part 7 of the Defence Regulations 2026 (for example on a placement outside a Defence workplace)
      `a respondent would run the Defence process and no one else can` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who harassed you would be involved in conducting the Part 7 process, and no one else is authorised to conduct it instead
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for a stop sexual harassment order as a defence member` IS
    IF (NOT `I was a defence member when it happened`) THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF    `a respondent was not a defence member then`
            OR `a respondent is not a defence member now`
            OR `my Defence review request got no direction or one I am dissatisfied with`
            OR `I am not eligible for the Defence Part 7 process`
            OR `a respondent would run the Defence process and no one else can`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `reg 4.01 -- the small claims procedure (only if you are suing in a magistrates court or the Federal Circuit Court)`

-- Reg 4.01(1): "the manner in which a person must indicate that the person wants a small claims procedure to apply ...
-- is: (a) by: (i) endorsing the papers initiating the action with a statement that the person wants a small claims
-- procedure to apply ...; or (ii) lodging with the [court] a paper that identifies the action and states that the person
-- wants a small claims procedure to apply ...; and (b) by serving a copy of the papers initiating the action, together
-- with a copy of the paper (if any) mentioned in subparagraph (a)(ii), on every other party". (2): "Subregulation (1)
-- does not apply ... if rules of court relating to that court prescribe the manner": NOTHING then (the court's rules
-- decide). Otherwise the manner is defined ("is"), so not meeting it is JUST FALSE.
@export Have I asked for the small claims procedure in the way the regulations require (s 548, reg 4.01(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `my court's rules prescribe how to ask` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of your court prescribe how to ask for the small claims procedure
      `I endorsed my initiating papers with the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your initiating papers carry a statement that you want the small claims procedure to apply
      `I lodged a separate paper asking for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a separate paper with the court identifying the action and saying you want the small claims procedure
      `I served the initiating papers on every other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you served a copy of the initiating papers on every other party
      `I served the separate paper on every other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you lodged a separate paper: whether you served a copy of it on every other party too
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I asked for the small claims procedure properly` IS
    IF `my court's rules prescribe how to ask` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    (   `I endorsed my initiating papers with the request`
                    OR `I lodged a separate paper asking for it`)
               AND `I served the initiating papers on every other party`
               AND ((NOT `I lodged a separate paper asking for it`) OR `I served the separate paper on every other party`))

DECLARE `Small claims court` IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2)`
    `a magistrates court`

-- Reg 4.01(3): in the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) a party "may be represented by an official of an
-- industrial association if the party is granted leave to do so"; (4): in a magistrates court "if: (a) the party is
-- granted leave ...; and (b) the law of the State allows a party to be represented in that court, in the circumstances
-- mentioned in paragraph (a), by officials of bodies representing interests related to the matters in dispute."
@export Can a union or employer association official represent me in my small claims case (s 548(8), reg 4.01(3)-(4))?
GIVEN `my court` IS A `Small claims court` @desc Which court is hearing the small claim: the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) or a magistrates court
      `if the court grants me leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court grants you leave to be represented by an industrial association official
      `my State's law allows such officials to represent in that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a magistrates court: whether your State's law lets officials of bodies representing interests related to the dispute represent a party there
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an industrial association official represent me` IF
    CONSIDER `my court`
    WHEN `the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2)` THEN `if the court grants me leave`
    WHEN `a magistrates court` THEN `if the court grants me leave` AND `my State's law allows such officials to represent in that court`

§ `regs 6.01A, 6.01B -- other proceedings that bar an unfair deactivation or termination application (only if you are a deactivated or terminated regulated worker)`

DECLARE `Other law` IS ONE OF
    `Chapter 6 of the Industrial Relations Act 1996 (NSW)`
    `the Owner Drivers and Forestry Contractors Act 2005 (Vic)`
    `Chapter 10A of the Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld)`
    `the Owner-Drivers (Contracts and Disputes) Act 2007 (WA)`
    `some other law`

-- Regs 6.01A, 6.01B: for the definitions of other deactivation proceedings (s 734BA(3)) and other termination proceedings
-- (s 734BB(3)) of the Act, "proceedings are specified if the proceedings are: (a) commenced by or on behalf of the
-- person who has been deactivated [terminated]; and (b) in relation to the deactivation [termination]; and (c) commenced
-- under any of the following" four State laws (including any other provision of the NSW or Qld Act so far as it relates
-- to the named Chapter). The answer is whether the other proceedings are of the specified kind; what follows from that
-- (the bar on a second application) is in ss 734BA, 734BB of the Act.
@export Are my other proceedings about my deactivation or termination of the kind that can stop an unfair deactivation or termination application (regs 6.01A, 6.01B)?
GIVEN `I or someone for me started them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other proceedings were started by you or on your behalf
      `they are about the deactivation or termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are about the same deactivation or termination
      `the law they were started under` IS AN `Other law` @desc The law under which they were started: NSW Industrial Relations Act 1996 Chapter 6, Victorian Owner Drivers and Forestry Contractors Act 2005, Queensland Industrial Relations Act 2016 Chapter 10A, WA Owner-Drivers (Contracts and Disputes) Act 2007, or some other law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my other proceedings specified` IF
        `I or someone for me started them`
    AND `they are about the deactivation or termination`
    AND (NOT (`the law they were started under` EQUALS `some other law`))
